\tag{frap}
\title{Transfer and the effect of dimension}

\p{The [orientation character](frap-000S) cancels changes of local
frames. Finite-index transfer uses the same cancellation for coset
representatives \citet{Sections 3.1--3.3}{mayer2015artin}.
The first section identifies the connection through an actual
transitive action and its stabilizer. The second computes how the
local rotation groups of simplices and cubes change with dimension,
following \citet{Sections 4--5}{marchetti2025rubik}.}

\transclude{frap-0012}
\transclude{frap-0013}
